get.summary:
Failed members: whether each is fenced (and the evidence), or why Apelora waits; and per
instance whether it restarts on another server (and where) or waits (and why). Read-only;
needs `cluster.view`.

Public. Reports that the service answers, the inventory provider, the authentication mode
and whether Incus is reachable. Incus is asked at most every 15 s whatever the request rate;
versions and error text are only on `GET /api/v1/system` (signed in).

architectures.description:
Architectures the image is known to run on, as Incus names them (`x86_64`, `aarch64`, …);
empty allows any.
Checked against the cluster before creating and against the instance Incus created.
